==English==

===Etymology===
First attested around 1852, in the US, as a fanciful alteration of the noun {{m|en|lick}} “a very fast sprint”, and the verb {{m|en|split}}. The forms {{m|en|lickety-cut}} and {{m|en|licketie}} are attested earlier. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-lickety-split.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|head=[[lickety]]-[[split]]|-}}

# [[quickly|Quickly]]; as [[fast]] as possible; in short order.
#: ''At the sound of the starting gun, they were off and running '''lickety-split'''.''

